    "language": "Let's see. So the first state, the moving to the left side of the field, appears to be correct. Though- though it must be clear that it doesn't have to be on the... You don't, you are not just limited to the left side of the field. You're also allowed to proceed to the right side of the field. And then the transition period in which you're waiting to team, for the teammate to pass the ball, that seems to be a proper transition. Okay. The... When you're stopping and receiving the ball, that's also... Seems to be correct as well. The transition period, uh, doesn't seem to be, uh, an actual transition period. It seems to be an a- uh, an ac- another action taking place, which is not supposed to be taking place a- a- as it's an actual transition period and not an action. So, in order to fix that, you might need to take a momentary pause and then pass to the teammate. In the third state, which is passing to your teammate.",
